{"id":"f1b20720c6db9b0a","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-lem-rr.md","title":"Recursion Theorem","display":"lem-rr — Recursion Theorem","type":"lemma","metadata":{"type":"lemma","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-lem-rr","aliases":["58-lem-rr"],"display":"lem-rr — Recursion Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-function]]","[[58-df-ordinal]]","[[58-thm-replacement]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"lemma"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-lem-rr"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-lem-rr</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"lem-rr — Recursion Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"58-df-ordinal\">58-df-ordinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0849bf4363d60a31\" href=\"?note=0849bf4363d60a31\" title=\"58-thm-replacement\">58-thm-replacement</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\\in V\">\\(\\theta\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(G:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}rr} \\vdash \\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\theta)\\land\\forall g\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(g,\\operatorname{dom}(g),\\operatorname{ran}(g))\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\operatorname{dom}(g))\\land\\operatorname{dom}(g)\\subseteq\\theta\\to\\exists!y\\;G(g,y)\\right)\\to\\exists!f\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(f,\\theta,\\operatorname{ran}(f))\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\theta\\;G(f\\upharpoonright\\alpha,f(\\alpha))\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}rr} \\vdash \\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\theta)\\land\\forall g\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(g,\\operatorname{dom}(g),\\operatorname{ran}(g))\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\operatorname{dom}(g))\\land\\operatorname{dom}(g)\\subseteq\\theta\\to\\exists!y\\;G(g,y)\\right)\\to\\exists!f\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(f,\\theta,\\operatorname{ran}(f))\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\theta\\;G(f\\upharpoonright\\alpha,f(\\alpha))\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The recursion theorem enables definitions by recursion.</li>\n<li>Any functional class rule on earlier stages yields a unique function on the specified ordinal.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ordinal","status":"resolved","id":"5582a281f15a33c2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location"